  "scope": "Room approach, first training run: 256 environments, each a random 3-5 m room with 1-3 furniture boxes; per episode a 0.30 x 0.28 x 0.90 m cabinet (2-4 kg) stands on the floor at a random free pose and the robot starts 1-3.5 m away at a random heading, without load. Every 0.1 s PPO sets the GR00T walk forward speed (-0.15-0.3 m/s), lateral speed (+-0.15 m/s) and yaw rate (+-0.3 rad/s) from the goal pose and A* look-ahead points in its heading frame plus local obstacle distances. Success: the robot root within 4 cm and 6 degrees of the pre-grasp pose (cabinet centre straight ahead at the grasp reach) at under 0.05 m/s, without pushing the cabinet more than 3 cm; walking above 0.3 m/s is penalized. A scripted pursuit-and-docking controller is evaluated on the same seeded starts. Lateral and backward GR00T walking are untested outside this training."
